From 5e0021e1e8c90a5f37aa53fa74af9543dc966bb3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrien Delmas <adrien@adriendelmas.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 08:28:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 154/160] wetmap: AO traced against raycast-visible objects
 only (S1)

Wet map (addition, docs/WETMAP_PLAN.md). The Ambient Occlusion node gets a
'Raycast Visibility' toggle: its rays are then tested against the objects
visible to raycast rays, the bit the Raycast node already traces with,
instead of every shadow-opaque object. Cycles 5.3 has no free visibility
bit (PATH_RAY_VISIBILITY_RAYCAST took the eighth), so the target set is the
raycast visibility, which the delegate now exposes per prim as
cycles:object:visibility:raycast ('Raycast Rays' in the Render Geometry
Settings). The OSL node carries the flag through the swidth texture option.

Measured with tools/bench_wet.py --gpu, 10/10 on CPU and OptiX: a probe
0.1 in front of a wide raycast-visible plane reads AO 0.011 (0.01 by the
geometry), 0.996 / 0.999 when the plane's raycast visibility is off, 0.011
again with the toggle off (control), 0.999 in front of a plane hidden from
every ray type. bench_render.py 97 rendered, bench_diff.py 0 regressions.
